{"question_id":"nzFCxAyY4jwP8rrB","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2012","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"alcohols-phenols-and-ethers","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"properties-preparation-and-uses-of-phenols","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"orthonitrophenol-is-less-soluble-in-water-than-p-and-m-2012-marks-4-nzfcxayy4jwp8rrb.htm","content":"Ortho\u2013Nitrophenol is less soluble in water than p\u2013 and m\u2013 Nitrophenols because :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"o\u2013Nitrophenol is more volatile in steam than those of m \u2013 and p\u2013isomers"},{"identifier":"B","content":"o\u2013Nitrophenol shows Intramolecular H\u2013bonding"},{"identifier":"C","content":"o\u2013Nitrophenol shows Intermolecular H\u2013bonding"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Melting point of o\u2013Nitrophenol is lower than those of m\u2013and p\u2013isomers."}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"As in ortho-Nitrophenol H of -OH is already in Intra-moleculer H Bond and become stable so it will not perticipate in H bonding with H<sub>2</sub>O by breaking this H bonding. That is why solublity of Ortho\u2013Nitrophenol is less in water.\n<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/3xmhtm2xjkbg2hr5r/5e92dd64-faac-40da-b279-3a8c843abdb3/7fdeb4f0-aeca-11ea-9207-bfdf7589d371/file-3xmhtm2xjkbg2hr5s-320w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2012 Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 183 English Explanation 1\">\n<br><br>para\u2013 and meta\u2013 Nitrophenols both shows inter-moleculer H bonding with H<sub>2</sub>O. That is why both are more soluble in water.\n<picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/3xmhtm2xjkbg2ubhe/30b86fe1-1907-4792-923d-7771bf92af03/dd478f30-aecb-11ea-9207-bfdf7589d371/file-3xmhtm2xjkbg2ubhf-320w.jpg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/3xmhtm2xjkbg2ubhe/30